### Protocol 

Protocol is set of rules and instructions 

Protocol method must not have bodies, it's same like Interface in Java, like we only have a blueprint of variables and functions

protocol LoginProtocol {
    func login(username: String, password: String)
}

class Login: LoginProtocol{
    
    func name(username: String, password: String){
                
    }
    
}

We can achieve Abstraction and Dependency Inversion and protocol oriented programming

protocol CarContract {
    func start()
}

protocol CarServiceContract {
    func carService()
}

class Car: CarContract , CarServiceContract{
    
    func carService(){
        
    }
    
    func start(){
        injectFuel()
        startEnging()
        checkSensor()
    }
    
    func injectFuel(){
        print("Inject Fuel")
    }
    
    func startEnging(){
        print("Start Engine")
    }
    
    func checkSensor(){
        print("Check Sensor")
    }
    
}


let car : CarContract = Car()

car.start()

Now the above whole code can be converted to Protocol, becuase the above functionality is exposing the functions


